   "subject": "Re: camtrapR",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Heidi,<br>assuming your GPS returns standard lat/long coordinates using the WGS84 ellipsoid (normally the default) it is<br><pre style=\"background-color:rgb(247,247,247);border-radius:3px;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre-wrap;margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:10px;padding:10px;font-size:14px\"><code style=\"border-radius:3px;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:11.9px\">shapefileProjection &lt;-<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\"> &quot;+proj=longlat +ellps=WGS84 +datum=WGS84 +no_defs&quot;</span></code></pre>See here: <a href=\"http://spatialreference.org/ref/epsg/4326/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://spatialreference.org/ref/epsg/4326/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792452075605000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CpByO4UU3Kp6qd-cNuT1X\">http://spatialreference.org/ref/epsg/4326/</a>   (go to &quot;Proj4&quot;)<br>Regards,<br>Jürgen<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
